<title>JAPAN: Stock ratings list - Nomura Securities (Apr 8).</title>
<headline>Stock ratings list - Nomura Securities (Apr 8).</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Follows is a list of ratings on Tuesday by Nomura Securities Co Ltd.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Rating unchanged:</p>
<p>Ryohin Keikaku Co Ltd -- &quot;1&quot;</p>
<p>Rohm Co Ltd -- &quot;1&quot;</p>
<p>Hac Kimisawa Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Yoshinoya D&amp;C Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Ryoyo Electro Corp -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Nippon Trust Bank Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Chuo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Nippon Light Metal Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Nintendo Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Marubeni Corp -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Shindengen Electric Manufacturing Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Aeon Credit Service Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Casio Computer Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The securities house assigns ratings as follows:</p>
<p>&quot;1&quot; - issues expected to outperform the key 225-share Nikkei average by more than 10 percentage points over the following six months.</p>
<p>&quot;2&quot; - issues seen moving within 10 percentage points in either direction of the key 225-share Nikkei average over the next six months.</p>
<p>&quot;3&quot; - issues expected to underperform the key 225-share Nikkei average by more than 10 percentage points over the following six months.</p>
